The Track B escape does not survive the required in-context attack. For any selection of the paper’s identities, a constant operation table satisfies every substitution; even banning constants does not help, because an abelian group table satisfies every generalized Bol–Moufang identity in the paper. I’m quantifying that shortcut against exhaustive substitution and documenting the rejection rather than manufacturing an unrelated completion/CSP problem.
