Rejected after full-text triage. The proposed family passes generation and exact verification, but fails hardness on both tracks.

A constant Cayley table satisfies every identity in the paper, giving an `O(n²)` deterministic construction. The same issue survives common restrictions: cyclic-group tables are nonconstant Latin squares satisfying all listed generalized identities. Thus the required in-context attack succeeds on every instance. The paper itself only enumerates orders 2–4 and provides no scalable hard regime. [Paper PDF](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2006.10650)

I documented the gate analysis, alternative formulations, and measured costs in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2006.10650/REJECTED.md). No generator or hardening artifacts were created, as required when H fails at Step 0.
